        "text": "Watch this video and listen to the English speech. Transcribe it with\ntimestamps, then translate it into natural Arabic (Egyptian Arabic\nwith simple, conversational wording).\n\nRULES FOR TECHNICAL TERMS:\n- Keep these in English exactly as written, in Latin letters, and do NOT\n  translate or transliterate them: pipelines, CI/CD, GitHub, Docker, Kubernetes, commit, branch, pull request, deploy, API, repo, build,\n  workflow, YAML, and any tool, product, command, or code name.\n- Keep any term that is normally said in English by Arabic developers.\n- Translate everything else into Arabic.\n- Never put Arabic letters inside an English term, or the reverse.\n\nKeep the Arabic about the same length as the English so it fits the same\ntiming. Return ONLY valid JSON, with no markdown and no extra text:\n{\"title\":\"...\",\"segments\":[{\"start\":0.0,\"end\":3.2,\"en\":\"...\",\"ar\":\"...\"}]}",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "5195ba05-4bdc-4bcb-9a24-5b5fd7eee7be",
      "name": "Gemini: Transcribe + Translate",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -160,
        464
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googlePalmApi": {
          "id": "MZ1lQrQxxt1bukxf",
          "name": "Google Gemini(PaLM) Api account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Read Gemini output (handles both node output shapes)\nconst item = $input.first().json;\nlet raw = item.content?.parts?.[0]?.text\n  ?? item.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text\n  ?? item.text\n  ?? '';\n\n// Strip markdown fences if Gemini added them\nraw = raw.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();\n\nconst data = JSON.parse(raw);\nconst segments = data.segments || [];\nconst fullText = segments.map(s => s.ar).join(' ');\n\nreturn [{ json: { title: data.title || 'dubbed', segments, fullText } }];"
      },
